{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Shared by the generator (scripts/sim), the Rust convergence test (src-tauri/tests/sim_convergence_tests.rs) and the e2e expectations.",
    "targets: imported stats in percent (stats::PlayerStats keys) with an absolute tolerance in percentage points, for cash 6-max at the sample sizes of the convergence test.",
    "expected.reads: the engine top read (strategic-analysis build) once the player is past min_hands, as the rule ids (with their chip tags) that may rank first for this profile; context facts (ctx.*, e.g. DEEP) are left out of the comparison. For the tilting player it is the read during a tilt episode (expected.during). expected.accepted: the further rule ids the pro read oracle (docs/specs/opponent-engine.md, section 16) accepts in the first two reads in cash and Zoom (tournament.expected.accepted: in its MTT rows); a guard in sim_matrix_tests keeps reads and accepted equal to the oracle.",
    "behaviour: decision ranges as a share of all starting hands (top X%) and postflop frequencies; see scripts/sim/lib/play.mjs.",
    "stakes.mtt / stakes.spin: tournament structures in chips (levels [sb, bb, ante]; buyIn components in cents, three of them for a knockout). avgStackBb is the field's average stack per level, used for villains moved in mid-tournament; a profile's tournament.stackBb overrides it (the short stack always arrives short). tournament.behaviour overrides behaviour in tournaments only (shove: open-shove range at 15bb or less); tournament.expected is the engine read once he is past min_hands, in the push/fold context.",
    "engineTargets.<format>: the read profiles' engine stats (engine::StatKey names in cash; late_* and ko_* replay splits in mtt) with absolute tolerances in percentage points, held by sim_convergence_tests (cash) and sim_formats_tests (mtt, --late-share 0.8). The read profiles play their own corpora (--profiles), apart from the baseline ones. An empty expected.reads is the oracle's (none): no cash read. tournament.late overrides behaviour at an MTT table whose average stack is under 20bb; tournament.expected.context names the hand the tournament read is checked in (push_fold, late or knockout). Expected reads come from the section-16 oracle of docs/specs/opponent-engine.md, written before any engine run."
  ],
